\subsection{One probe for tip and branch}
\label{sec:head-state}

Every Git call costs a fork and an exec before Git reads a byte, and
for the one-object commands of this protocol that startup \emph{is}
the cost.
The run protocol asks [[HEAD]] two questions---does a commit exist at
all (\cref{sec:init-repo}), and which branch at which tip is the next
commit to build on---and [[git rev-parse]] happens to answer both in
one process: given a revision and [[--symbolic-full-name]] it prints
the hash and the ref, one per line, in argument order.

The three states of \cref{sec:recording-branch} come out as three
shapes of output.
Attached, the probe prints the hash and the full ref.
Detached, [[--symbolic-full-name]] echoes the literal [[HEAD]] it
was given instead of naming a branch---which is why the parse below
demands a [[refs/]] prefix rather than settling for a second
line.
Unborn, the whole command fails, because the hash half has nothing
to resolve; that non-zero exit is [[has_commit]]'s answer, so the
probe runs with [[check=False]].

<<repo methods>>=
def head_state(self):
    """Return ``(tip, branch)`` for ``HEAD`` in one Git call.

    `tip` is the commit `HEAD` resolves to, or `None` while the
    branch is unborn.  `branch` is the full ref `HEAD` points at,
    or `None` when `HEAD` is detached or unborn.
    """
    probe = self.git(
        "rev-parse", "HEAD", "--symbolic-full-name", "HEAD",
        check=False,
    )
    if probe.returncode != 0:
        return None, None
    lines = probe.stdout.splitlines()
    tip = lines[0].strip() if lines else ""
    branch = lines[1].strip() if len(lines) > 1 else ""
    if not branch.startswith("refs/"):
        branch = None
    return tip or None, branch
@

Both commits of a run start from this probe, through a helper that
settles what happens when there is no branch to read.
Detached, the branch comes from the ref listing as before
(\cref{sec:recording-branch}), but that branch's tip is \emph{not}
[[HEAD]]'s, so the helper answers [[RESOLVE_PARENT]] and leaves the
tip for [[commit_on_branch]] to look up
(\cref{sec:commit-on-branch}).
A helper rather than a shared chunk, because the two call sites are
different methods: a function makes the dependency on the sentinel
explicit at both.

<<repo methods>>=
def branch_and_expected_tip(self):
    """Return the recording branch and the tip to build on.

    The tip is `RESOLVE_PARENT` when `HEAD` is detached or
    unborn, where `HEAD`'s tip does not answer for the branch.
    """
    tip, branch = self.head_state()
    if branch is None:
        return self.recording_branch(), RESOLVE_PARENT
    return branch, tip
@

Let's verify the probe reads all three states correctly, and that
the helper falls back to the ref listing when [[HEAD]] is detached.
The unresolvable state is produced by deleting the branch ref under
an attached [[HEAD]], which leaves [[HEAD]] pointing at a branch
that no longer exists---the same shape as an unborn repository.

