important---leaves no lock file behind for the student's next
[[git add]] to trip over.
Staging a file at the end of the test is how we ask about both at once:
it fails if what we published is not an index Git will read, and it
fails if a lock of ours is still in the way.

<<test functions>>=
def test_publish_replaces_the_index_and_leaves_no_lock(workdir):
    """A publish that runs unopposed also cleans up after itself."""
    repo = LearnlogRepo(workdir)
    shared = repo.git_dir / SHARED_INDEX_NAME
    before = shared.read_bytes()
    (workdir / "extra.py").write_text("x = 1\n")
    repo.begin_run("hello.py", [], datetime.datetime.now())
    assert shared.read_bytes() != before
    assert not (repo.git_dir / SHARED_INDEX_LOCK_NAME).exists()
    repo.git("add", "extra.py")
@

The two outcomes have to be distinguishable from outside, and the only
place they can be told apart is the log.
A [[rename]] that fails is the one failure here with no benign reading,
so a run that hits it stays a recorded run---the header commit was made
before any of this---and says so where somebody can find it later:

<<test functions>>=
def test_a_failed_publish_is_recorded_in_the_errors_log(
        workdir, monkeypatch
):
    """A rename that fails is a defect, not a design decision."""
    repo = LearnlogRepo(workdir)

    def refuse(*args, **kwargs):
        raise OSError("no room on device")

    monkeypatch.setattr(os, "replace", refuse)
    repo.begin_run("hello.py", [], datetime.datetime.now())
    monkeypatch.undo()
    msg = repo.git("log", "-1", "--format=%B").stdout
    assert f"Run-Id: {repo.run_id}" in msg
    log = (repo.git_dir / ERRORS_LOG_NAME).read_text()
    assert "publish run index" in log
    assert "no room on device" in log
@

Whereas the skip we designed for writes nothing at all.
Asking for the log file to be absent rather than merely unchanged is
the stronger question: a log that exists is a log somebody will read,
and the first entry in it should never be one that means everything is
fine.

<<test functions>>=
def test_the_skipped_publish_says_nothing(workdir):
    """The lock-held skip is expected, so it stays silent."""
    repo = LearnlogRepo(workdir)
    (repo.git_dir / SHARED_INDEX_LOCK_NAME).write_text("")
    repo.begin_run("hello.py", [], datetime.datetime.now())
    assert not (repo.git_dir / ERRORS_LOG_NAME).exists()
