\section{Runs against a repository in an awkward state}
\label{sec:awkward-state}

The two states of \cref{sec:recording-branch} are ones the student
puts the repository into on purpose, and both used to change what a
run meant.
Since a run only sees them by accident---it starts when a program
starts, not when the repository is ready---the tests here set the
repository up the way the student would and then run a program
through it.

The first state is a conflicted merge.
Building one takes a commit that is not on the branch, which is what
[[learnlog pull]] fetches from another machine; the helper makes one
with the same plumbing \cref{sec:commit-on-branch} uses, so no second
work tree is needed.

<<test functions>>=
def _conflicted_merge(repo, workdir):
    """Leave the repository mid-merge, as a conflicted pull does.

    Returns the commit the merge is trying to bring in.
    """
    base = repo.git("rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip()
    (workdir / "hello.py").write_text('print("ours")\n')
    repo.begin_run(
        "hello.py", [], datetime.datetime(2026, 1, 1, 9, 0),
    )
    blob = repo.git(
        "hash-object", "-w", "--stdin",
        input='print("theirs")\n',
    ).stdout.strip()
    tree = repo.git(
        "mktree", input=f"100644 blob {blob}\thello.py\n",
    ).stdout.strip()
    theirs = repo.git(
        "commit-tree", tree, "-p", base, input="theirs\n",
    ).stdout.strip()
    repo.git("update-ref", "refs/heads/other", theirs)
    merged = repo.git("merge", "--no-edit", "other", check=False)
    assert merged.returncode != 0
    return theirs
@

A run recorded in that window must leave every part of the merge where
it found it, and its own two commits must have one parent each---a
second parent is what \enquote{learnlog resolved the conflict} looks
like in the history.
The code state it records is the work tree as it stands, conflict
markers and all, for the reason \cref{sec:beginning-a-run} gives, and
the diagnostic says so where a student can find it.

<<test functions>>=
def test_run_during_a_conflicted_merge_adds_one_parent(workdir):
    """A run must not conclude the student's merge for them."""
    repo = LearnlogRepo(workdir)
    branch = repo.recording_branch()
    theirs = _conflicted_merge(repo, workdir)

    running = LearnlogRepo(workdir)
    running.begin_run(
        "hello.py", [], datetime.datetime(2026, 1, 1, 10, 0),
    )
    running.finalize_run(
        io_log="stderr: SyntaxError\n",
        exception_info=None,
        end_time=datetime.datetime(2026, 1, 1, 10, 0, 1),
        exit_code=1,
    )

    trailer_parents = repo.git(
        "log", "-1", "--format=%P", branch,
    ).stdout.split()
    header_parents = repo.git(
        "log", "-1", "--format=%P", f"{branch}~1",
    ).stdout.split()
    assert len(trailer_parents) == 1
    assert len(header_parents) == 1

    assert (workdir / ".learnlog" / "MERGE_HEAD").exists()
    assert repo.git(
        "rev-parse", "MERGE_HEAD",
    ).stdout.strip() == theirs
    assert repo.git("ls-files", "-u").stdout.strip()
    assert "<<<<<<<" in (workdir / "hello.py").read_text()
    assert "<<<<<<<" in repo.git(
        "show", f"{branch}~1:hello.py",
    ).stdout
    errors = (
        workdir / ".learnlog" / "errors.log"
    ).read_text()
    assert "UnfinishedOperation" in errors
    assert "MERGE_HEAD" in errors
@

Those are the parts; the whole is whether the student can still
finish.
Concluding the merge is [[git commit]] with the conflict resolved, and
what comes out has to be a real merge commit: two parents, the second
being the commit that was being merged and the first the run that
happened in the meantime.

<<test functions>>=
def test_the_students_merge_can_still_be_concluded(workdir):
    """The half-finished merge survives a run and completes."""
    repo = LearnlogRepo(workdir)
    branch = repo.recording_branch()
    theirs = _conflicted_merge(repo, workdir)

    running = LearnlogRepo(workdir)
    running.begin_run(
        "hello.py", [], datetime.datetime(2026, 1, 1, 10, 0),
    )
    running.finalize_run(
        io_log="",
        exception_info=None,
        end_time=datetime.datetime(2026, 1, 1, 10, 0, 1),
        exit_code=1,
    )
    trailer = repo.git("rev-parse", branch).stdout.strip()

    (workdir / "hello.py").write_text('print("resolved")\n')
    repo.git("add", "hello.py")
    repo.git("commit", "--file=-", input="merged\n")

    parents = repo.git(
        "log", "-1", "--format=%P", branch,
    ).stdout.split()
    assert parents == [trailer, theirs]
    assert not (workdir / ".learnlog" / "MERGE_HEAD").exists()
