The second state is a detached [[HEAD]], which is what
[[learnlog git checkout]] leaves behind when a student goes to look at
an older version of their code.
The run afterwards has to reach the branch: [[git log --branches]] is
the set of commits [[learnlog push]] would send, so asking for the
run's records there is asking whether the run was pushable.
And [[HEAD]] has to still be where the student left it, because the
run is not entitled to undo their checkout.

